From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: retain exact O82 OEM PHY strength selection

Both exact O82 variants specify clk-strength=0xff with no deemphasis.
At the current admitted lane clock, OEM v5.2 DPHY selects SWI_CAL=1 and
HSTX_STR0=0xff. Preserve generic selection and override only these two
locals after the existing O82 board/D-PHY/link/rate admission succeeds.
Reuse the existing common writer. Other PHYs, timing bytes, voltages,
PLL, EOT, packet geometry and per-lane settings remain unchanged.

Sources: MiCode display44275c404a677d9d9e5230fedd1af2ef02fc7b9a,
msm/dsi/dsi_phy_hw_v5_0.c and dsi_phy.c; display-DT
4a3e1c391130237c5e8c2b250d1c94f3e25b9b11, both O82 variants.
GPL-2.0-only notices and Qualcomm/Linux Foundation attribution retained.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
@@ -1123,6 +1123,16 @@
 		glbl_rescode_bot_ctrl = 0x3c;
 	}
 
+	/* The earlier O82 timing admission validates board, D-PHY, id and rate.
+	 * Exact Uke v5.2 OEM selects this pair with clk-strength=ff and no
+	 * deemphasis; keep the existing common writer and other PHYs unchanged.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(phy->pdev->dev.of_node,
+				    "xiaomi,uke-o82-dsi-phy-4nm")) {
+		glbl_str_swi_cal_sel_ctrl = 0x01;
+		glbl_hstx_str_ctrl_0 = 0xff;
+	}
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&pll->pll_enable_lock, flags);
 	pll->pll_enable_cnt = 1;
 	/* de-assert digital and pll power down */
